<!-- Copy this to ~/.local/state/visionocr-autonomous/RUN.md before the first start:
       mkdir -p ~/.local/state/visionocr-autonomous
       cp ops/autonomous/RUN.md.template ~/.local/state/visionocr-autonomous/RUN.md
     It lives OUTSIDE the repo on purpose. It changes every session, so keeping it in the tree would
     churn commits for state that is not part of the project's history — and the things that ARE part of
     that history (the register, the queue, the changelog) are committed and pushed, so a fresh session
     still recovers everything that matters from git.

     ⚠️ The "RUN STATUS:" line above must stay a PLAIN greppable line. The daemon stops on
     `grep '^RUN STATUS: COMPLETE'`, so decorating it (`**RUN STATUS:**`) means COMPLETE can never be
     detected and the daemon never unloads. -->

