## NEEDS OWNER

<!-- The daemon's outbox. A session that hits something needing a human APPENDS here and moves on — it
     never waits, because nobody is awake to answer. `daemon.sh status` surfaces this under "Needs you".

     This is the half of the arrangement that makes unattended work safe: the run does not have to
     choose between guessing and stopping. Drain it when you check in. -->

## SESSION LOG

